/signal /social 301
/sonics /music 301

# /community's index moved into a section on /social (2026-08-21). Exact paths
# only, never /community/* — the wildcard would swallow /community/me and the
# /community/u/* rewrite below, which are still live pages. Both the bare and
# trailing-slash forms are listed because Astro's static output makes the
# trailing-slash form canonical and either can be linked from outside.
# The page file itself was deleted rather than left in place: on Pages a
# matching static asset wins over a redirect rule, so an index.html at
# /community would simply keep serving and this rule would never fire.
/community /social 301
/community/ /social 301

# Astro here is static output with no adapter, so a dynamic [handle].astro
# route can't prerender unknown fan handles. Instead every /community/u/*
# path is rewritten (200, not a redirect) to the same static shell, which
# reads the handle from location.pathname and fetches it client-side.
# Placed after the two 301s above and scoped to /community/u/* specifically
# so it cannot shadow /community itself or those existing redirects.
#
# Target must be the CANONICAL directory URL, with the trailing slash
# ("/community/profile/"), not the bare directory ("/community/profile")
# and not the literal asset file ("/community/profile/index.html").
#
# - Bare directory: Astro's static output emits this route as
#   dist/community/profile/index.html, so Cloudflare's asset server 308s a
#   bare-directory hit to add the trailing slash -- replacing the URL the
#   browser is showing and discarding the /community/u/<handle> path the
#   client script needs to read from location.pathname. This was the
#   original bug.
# - Literal index.html: looks like the obvious fix, but Cloudflare's own
#   redirect validator (and wrangler's local emulation of it) treats ANY
#   200-rewrite target ending in "index.html" as a potential infinite loop
#   and silently drops the entire rule at deploy time -- confirmed by
#   testing against `wrangler pages dev` here, and matches a known
#   upstream false-positive (cloudflare/workers-sdk#11824). A dropped rule
#   is worse than the original bug: every /community/u/* request falls
#   through with no rewrite at all.
# Requesting the already-canonical trailing-slash form avoids both: it
# doesn't end in "index.html" (so the loop heuristic doesn't fire) and it's
# already the form the asset server would redirect a bare directory TO, so
# there's nothing left to canonicalize and no 308 happens. Verified against
# `wrangler pages dev`: GET /community/profile/ -> 200, correct page, no
# redirect.
/community/u/* /community/profile/ 200
